window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"vladimir","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-5","text":"The whole lane is a cooldown chess match: Transfusion heals his nail chip, and Ashen Pursuit is his only mobility on a 10s timer - the ten seconds after he spends it is the window you fight in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Purgatory is 120s at rank 1 and executes below a threshold - stay above the floor, or spend Pool's 2 untargetable seconds inside the zone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"It stays close, but your sustain starts clawing the lane back - each Transfusion undoes his poke faster than he can reapply it."},{"when":"Late","text":"You outscale outright: Hemoplague amp plus drain-tank healing wins every extended fight his burst cannot end instantly."}],"wants":{"you":["Pool saved for his blink-in and the execute","Transfusion weaves that undo his nail chip","The long game where drain outscales burst"],"foe":["Baiting Pool, then Ashen Pursuit onto a marked you","R Purgatory placed while your Pool is down","Ending the game before Hemoplague takes over"]},"early":"Levels 1 to 6 are all even. Ritual Nails (10s) marks you from 950, and his autos consume those marks for bonus damage, while Silver Stake adds on-hit magic damage that grows as your health drops. Transfusion heals the nail damage back, and Tides of Blood hits him from 600. Ashen Pursuit (10s) teleports and dashes him onto you, so trade in the 10 seconds after he uses it. Soul Ignition (18s) makes him faster but burns his own health before healing some back, so kite it out. At 6 Purgatory (120s) can execute you below a health threshold, so stay above it.","mid":"Nothing separates you through 4-6 unless someone blinks: he wants marks on you, then Ashen Pursuit in for the bite, with Purgatory to execute what is left. Hold Sanguine Pool's 2 seconds for exactly that arrival, heal everything else, and Soul Ignition's self-damage window is where Grievous Wounds pays.","late":"First item stays close but the current has turned - your sustain claws back every trade, and from two items on you simply outscale him: Hemoplague's amp turns fights into team-wide executions, Pool laughs at his totem timing, and drain-tank healing grinds through burst that no longer one-rotations you.","whys":["An even skill lane at 1 - his burst threat and your escape tools cancel out.","Trades stay balanced around your Pool and Transfusion cooldowns at 2.","Level 3 remains a skill fight over whether he can bait out your escapes.","Neither side pulls clearly ahead through levels 4-5.","At 6 your untargetable Pool trades evenly against his execute totem.","First item stays close, but your sustain begins clawing the lane back.","Late, your drains and Hemoplague amp outscale his burst completely."]});
