window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"vladimir","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-5","text":"A long even stretch: your Transfusion sustain and E zoning offset his Q The Darkin Glaive poke, and neither of you can force a kill without the other misplaying."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hemoplague amp versus his R Grim Deliverance is pure execution - it heals him off the damage, so land anti-heal before your ult swings the fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first AP item is the takeover point: Q and E become real burst, and Sanguine Pool now dodges the all-in he needs to land to stay relevant."},{"when":"2 items","text":"You are a full drain-tank - Pool plus spell-vamp healing means his bruiser DPS can no longer race your sustain, so take every extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Safe scaling into your first AP item","Pool timed onto his R Grim Deliverance","Extended fights where drain beats bruiser DPS"],"foe":["Kill pressure before your item spike lands","E Aureate Rush burst while Pool is down","A short game that ends before you outscale"]},"early":"Levels 1 to 6 are an even lane. The Darkin Glaive (10s) slashes twice and heals Zaahen, and its recast knocks you up. Dreaded Return (14s) stabs from 850 and pulls you in, so stand off its line and heal the Q damage back with Transfusion. Aureate Rush (10s) is his only dash, so trade in the ten seconds after he uses it. Cultivation of War stacks give him AD the longer he fights champions, so keep your trades short and walk away before he fills the bar. At 6 Grim Deliverance heals him off its damage, so hold Pool for it.","mid":"Level 6 changes the stakes but not the balance: Hemoplague turns any extended fight your way, while his R Grim Deliverance heals him back through a mistimed Pool - whoever lands their ultimate on their own terms wins the all-in, so play it patient and make him move first.","late":"Your first AP item is where the lane tips for good - Q and E become genuine burst and Pool invalidates the all-in window he spent all lane building toward. By two items you are a scaling drain-tank he cannot solve: his Q and R healing lose the race once Grievous Wounds is on him, and Hemoplague ends his teamfights.","whys":["Level 1 is an even poke lane with no committal tools online for either side.","Level 2 stays neutral - you trade pokes but neither of you can commit.","Level 3 is a skill fight: your Q poke and Transfusion sustain offset his glaive, and your E zoning holds the line.","Levels 4-5 remain a skill check - your low base HP and his burst balance against your healing.","Level 6 stays even: your Hemoplague amp versus his R lockdown comes down to execution.","On your first AP item you spike ahead - Q and E become real burst and Pool dodges his all-in.","Two items in you are a scaling drain-tank whose Pool and lifesteal make you the stronger sustained duelist."]});
