window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"vladimir","b":"masteryi","win":["Vladimir","Vladimir","Vladimir","Vladimir","Master Yi","Master Yi","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-4","text":"You farm him for breakfast: Transfusion pokes and heals on one button, and Alpha Strike is 20s at rank 1 — his only engage, and Pool answers it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Highlander is 85s and makes him immune to slows, so Tides of Blood and Pool's slow do nothing to stop him - keep Pool for the commit itself, not his approach."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Wuju Style adds true damage to every attack, so armour and MR buy you nothing here - play far back, stack health, and never show without Pool available."},{"when":"Late","text":"Your healing balloons past his DPS: a pooled Alpha Strike, Hemoplague's burst heal, and drain sustain make you the duelist he can no longer race."}],"wants":{"you":["Free Transfusion chip on his itemless levels","Pool held for the Highlander commit","Scaled fights where Hemoplague out-heals his DPS"],"foe":["A quiet lane into his first item spike","Highlander dives, immune to all your slows","Killing you before your late-game healing arrives"]},"early":"Levels 1 to 5 are yours. Alpha Strike (20s) is Master Yi's only engage, and it is a short burst that one Transfusion heals back. Meditate (10s) heals him, but he stands still while channeling, so charge Tides of Blood and hit him with it. Double Strike adds a second hit every few autos, so stand outside his auto range when you last-hit. Wuju Style (14s) adds true damage, but only if he reaches you. At 6 he is ahead: Highlander (85s) makes him immune to slows and speeds him onto you, so keep Pool for his commit.","mid":"At 6 he finally has teeth: Highlander is 85s, makes him slow-immune, and refreshes his cooldowns on a kill, so one won fight rolls straight into the next. This is his era - concede space, hold Pool strictly for the moment he commits, and buy Grievous Wounds before Meditate does the work.","late":"The scaling war ends in your favor: your ballooning drain healing plus Pool means his all-in no longer finishes you, and Hemoplague's amp-and-heal turns his own dive into your team's kill window - survive his mid-game spike and the last word in this lane is always yours.","whys":["Your Transfusion sustain and range out-trade him from level 1.","At 2 your healing beats Meditate and he has no way to punish you.","Level 3 Sanguine Pool dodges Alpha Strike so he can never engage cleanly.","Level 4 you keep poking and pooling every commit he attempts.","At 6 Highlander lets him dive and out-burst your Q healing.","His first item plus R drops you faster than Transfusion can heal.","Late, your ballooning healing, Pool and Hemoplague burst out-scale him again."]});
